From 649cd7206b8683384307462808e4ee4f11e0d2cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daedalao <daedalao@hotmail.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 03:01:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 09/16] cmd/go: implicit overlay supplying golang.org/x/sys
 files for linux/ppc

Upstream golang.org/x/sys ships no gc assembly for linux/ppc and no cpu
package support for ppc, so every module importing x/sys/unix or
x/sys/cpu fails to build for GOARCH=ppc. Until that lands upstream,
cmd/go adds an implicit overlay (fsys.Implicit) that supplies
misc/ppc/xsys/unix/asm_linux_ppc.s and misc/ppc/xsys/cpu/cpu_ppc.go to
copies of x/sys found in the module cache or a vendor directory, unless
the copy already ships the file. The module index hash and the compiler
invocation account for implicit entries; DirContainsReplacement ignores
them so they may live beneath GOMODCACHE.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0117Su2urNmg96oYM6vhHi1y
